Specification:
A worker starts a nested group of two tasks; the two inner tasks both need mutexes A and B and must not form a circular wait. Every interleaving must terminate and the outer worker must complete. On completion the program must print exactly one line `DONE done=1` and then exit; it must terminate.


Current program:
```rust
use std::sync::{mpsc, Arc, Condvar, Mutex};
use std::thread;

fn main() {
    let a = Arc::new(Mutex::new(()));
    let b = Arc::new(Mutex::new(()));
    let (a1, b1) = (Arc::clone(&a), Arc::clone(&b));
    let x1 = thread::spawn(move || {
        let _ga = a1.lock().unwrap();
        let _gb = b1.lock().unwrap();
    });
    let (a2, b2) = (Arc::clone(&a), Arc::clone(&b));
    let x2 = thread::spawn(move || {
        let _gb = b2.lock().unwrap();
        let _ga = a2.lock().unwrap();
    });
    x1.join().unwrap();
    x2.join().unwrap();
    println!("DONE done=1");
}

```

Fix any concurrency defect and output the complete corrected Rust program, or if there is none reply exactly NO_ISSUES.

